# No raw HTML form controls

Do **not** use native HTML form elements in app UI. Use the project's shadcn/ui wrappers from `@/components/ui/` (and existing field composites).

## Banned in JSX (use the replacement)

| Do not use | Use instead |
|------------|-------------|
| `<input>` (text, email, tel, number, search, password, …) | `Input`, `PasswordInput`, `CurrencyInput` |
| `<input type="date">` | `DatePickerField` |
| `<input type="datetime-local">` / date + time | `DateTimeField` |
| `<input type="time">` | `TimePickerField` or `DateTimeField` — never native time picker |
| `<input type="color">` | `ColorPickerField` |
| `<select>` / `<option>` | `Select` (+ `SelectTrigger`, `SelectContent`, `SelectItem`, …) or `ComboboxField` for searchable lists |
| `<textarea>` | `Textarea` |
| `<input type="checkbox">` | `Checkbox` (+ `Label`) |
| `<button>` for actions | `Button` |
| Native calendar / browser date UI | `Calendar` inside `Popover` via `DatePickerField` |

## Also avoid

- Raw `<input>` styled with `settingsField`, `adminField`, or ad-hoc `className` — wrap with `Input` / field components and apply shell tokens on the component.
- Re-introducing patterns we already replaced (e.g. inline `<input type="date">` on Quick Till, sales forms, settings).

## Allowed exceptions

- `type="hidden"` for non-visible form plumbing
- `type="file"` when no project file-picker component exists yet (prefer adding one if the UI is user-facing)
- Third-party libs that render their own DOM and cannot be swapped without a wrapper

## When adding new fields

1. Check `src/components/ui/` first.
2. If nothing fits, add a reusable component under `src/components/ui/` (shadcn pattern), then use it — do not drop a raw element into a page.
